# ── GHSA-c2c7-rcm5-vvqj (picomatch ReDoS via extglob) ─────────────────────────
# Affected packages:
#   - artifacts/api-server → vitest → @vitest/utils → picomatch >=4.0.0 <4.0.4
#   - artifacts/mockup-sandbox → fast-glob → micromatch → picomatch <2.3.2
#
# Risk assessment: LOW
#   - picomatch is used ONLY in the Vitest test runner (dev) and Vite build tool (dev).
#   - These packages are NOT bundled into or deployed as the production API server.
#   - An attacker would need to control glob patterns passed to test utilities,
#     which is not possible in our threat model (no user input reaches glob calls).
#   - Production attack surface: ZERO.
#
# Remediation status:
#   - vitest 3.2.4 (current) uses picomatch 4.0.x — fix available in 4.0.4.
#   - To fix: upgrade vitest when 3.2.5+ is released with picomatch >=4.0.4.
